note Built the RegressionFence rather than touching FPQ, because the archive's central lesson is that "fix FPQ" is a prohibited vague mission. The material contribution is the mechanism that governs FPQ, not FPQ. All FPQ-specific claims here are recorded at MEASURED at most, from the archive, not re-run by this process.

work proof_frontier_wire_into_fence
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 8.0
  reason proof_frontier.py works and is seeded for Qwen-0.5B FPQ: three proven layers, open at transformer_math, three known non-causes. Next is making authorize_mutation a real gate a model-editing mission must pass, not a library call. It belongs in the same admission position as resource and provider checks

work fpq_verify_archive_claims_before_promoting
  target_plane run5_recursive_external
  priority 7.5
  reason Every FPQ frontier entry is asserted from the archive at the measured plane. The FP16-passthrough and Q/K/V-bypass experiments should be re-run and turned into golden fixtures before any invariant moves to the proven plane. Until then a reheat condition -- reconstruction fixture fails -- has nothing to fire against

work fpq_split_sli_identity
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason SLI is two concepts under one name: Structured Layer Inference (the public BonfyreSLI) and Spectral Lattice Inference (FPQ direct execution). Do not rename the command; disambiguate the profiles beneath it -- sli.structured-layer/v1 and fpq.spectral-lattice-execution/v1 -- so a receipt says which ran

work fpq_representation_is_not_identity
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 7.0
  reason Model identity, representation profile, prepared SLI state, execution phenotype and runtime capability have historically leaked into each other, which is why changing one silently invalidated another. A ModelPassport that binds them, and separate invalidation domains, is the structural fix. FPQ is representation, never identity

work representation_cut_generalization
  target_plane run4_institutional_fabric
  priority 6.0
  reason The archive's deepest claim is that FPQ, Context Cut and Habitat are three scales of one operation: source state to basis plus residual plus witness, executed as a phenotype, measured against a purpose-relative divergence. Worth testing whether the ProofFrontier machinery already generalizes -- the Bernstein test says the fence does; the basis-residual-witness reduction itself is the larger open question

work proof_frontier_over_agentguard_218
  target_plane run2_relationship_adoption
  priority 6.5
  reason A live test of the fence outside FPQ: agentguard 218's portable-paths regression is a proven-below-open situation. The inverse resolver is the open layer; the structural validation from 229 is proven and off-limits. The fence would encode exactly the boundary the maintainer drew by hand

work knownnoncause_for_every_diagnosis
  target_plane run5_recursive_external
  priority 5.5
  reason This session eliminated several hypotheses by experiment -- the probe pipe deadlock, the acronym manifest, the vacuous 214 regression, the Proton client-vs-account block. Each is a KnownNonCause worth recording, so the next worker subtracts them rather than rediscovering them
